Inherited / derived from the original
-------------------------------------
- firmware/wifi_manager.py
    Origin: WiFiManager by Igor Ferreira (MIT license, see file header),
    modified by Elektroarzt, further adapted here
    (MQTT removed; password confirm/"show"; SSID refresh; OTA in AP mode;
     auto-redirect; watchdog feeding).
- SCPI startup sequence / UART handling in firmware/app.py
    (idle check, *IDN? handshake, "RATE F" fast mode, logging idea)
    conceptually originates from the original main.py.
- Hardware concept & wiring (OWON UART <-> ESP), plus the KiCad PCB
    (production/) and assets/, from the original.


New in this variant (own work)
------------------------------
- Port from ESP32-C3 to ESP32-WROOM (UART2 GPIO16/17).
- Complete web dashboard (app.py): tabs/sub-modes, side toolbar,
  live graph with axes, min/max/avg, themes (export/import),
  display/network settings, unit mode, factory reset.
- JSON REST API under /api.
- OTA system (ota.py): streaming upload, web console; OTA in ALL modes
  (app, recovery, setup-AP).
- Reliability: watchdog (wd.py), boot counter, full-set golden-snapshot
  rollback (good/), recovery server (recovery.py), logging (dbg.py).
- Robust launcher/bootloader (main.py).
- PyVISA/SCPI-TCP server (port 5025), in parallel with the web UI.
- Tools: flash.sh (USB first-flash + OTA with device selection),
  pyvisa_test.py.

The original's MQTT/Home Assistant integration is NOT used here.


Thanks to Elektroarzt and Igor Ferreira for the groundwork.
